# Premium Infographic Generation

When creating or replacing ExpatLife infographics, use the high-end editorial image-generation approach. Do not default to code-generated SVG/PNG templates for premium pillar pages.

## Benchmark Style

Use existing premium double-taxation assets as the quality benchmark:

- `apps/expatlife-web/public/images/infographics/netherlands-double-taxation-treaty-premium-v1.png`
- `apps/expatlife-web/public/images/infographics/netherlands-double-taxation-residency-premium-v1.png`
- `apps/expatlife-web/public/images/infographics/netherlands-double-taxation-foreign-income-premium-v1.png`
- `apps/expatlife-web/public/images/infographics/netherlands-double-taxation-mistakes-premium-v1.png`

Target the same editorial quality: rich Dutch city/canal context, realistic desk or consultation scenes, detailed props, textured illustration, shadows, clear information hierarchy, right-side record/checklist rails, bottom skyline/water band, and ExpatLife branding.

## Required Workflow

1. Inspect the page model and list every visual key that needs an asset.
2. Design a unique concept per section before generating images.
3. Use `GenerateImage` with 1-3 benchmark reference images.
4. Save assets with a new version suffix such as `premium-v6`; do not overwrite old versions unless intentionally regenerating the same filename.
5. Copy generated files into `apps/expatlife-web/public/images/infographics/`.
6. Update page-model `src` references only after the image exists.
7. Run lints on edited model files and verify referenced assets exist.

## Prompt Requirements

Every prompt should specify:

- `1024x768 landscape`
- Page/topic and exact title/subtitle text
- Section-specific concept, not a generic dashboard
- Concrete user-helpful labels, numbers, examples, scenarios or records
- Dutch visual context, premium navy/teal/white palette, and ExpatLife brand area
- Brand footer: gold compass icon + wordmark **ExpatLife** + tagline **Live. Love. Stay.** only (match double-taxation benchmark). Never draw website addresses, domains, or TLD suffixes anywhere in the image — especially **not** `www.expatlife.nl`, `expatlife.nl`, `.nl`, `.eu`, `.com`, or `expatcopilot.com`
- In image-generation prompts, describe branding **positively only**. Never write literal negative instructions such as "NO", "do not show .eu", or "without ExpatLife.eu" — models may render that text into the artwork. Instead say what **should** appear: compass icon, **ExpatLife**, **Live. Love. Stay.**
- Use positive disclaimer copy in sidebars (e.g. "General information only" / "Verify with providers") instead of large "No advice" callouts unless the section concept requires it
- Safety constraints such as no legal/tax/financial advice guarantees, no fake ratings, no fake official logos

## Variety Rules

Do not generate a batch where every image shares the same composition. Mix layouts such as:

- record-file builders
- map and treaty bridges
- timeline/calendar flows
- desk scenes with documents
- advisor consultation scenes
- city or route maps
- checklist and mistake boards
- ecosystem diagrams
- provider/service maps

## Rejection Criteria

Regenerate any image that has:

- flat SVG-template appearance
- low-detail generic icons
- repeated composition across many sections
- unreadable or malformed title text
- misleading legal/tax/financial claims
- fabricated awards, reviews, rankings or guarantees
- wrong section concept despite the correct filename
- stray footer titles or off-brand copy that changes the page meaning
- domain extensions, website URLs, or TLD suffixes in ExpatLife branding (including `www.expatlife.nl`, `expatlife.nl`, or any `.nl` / `.com` / `.eu` text in the footer)
- literal negative prompt text baked into artwork ("NO", "do not show", domain names used as rejection labels)

## Verification

Before final response, confirm:

- each referenced image path exists
- no rejected version remains referenced
- page models point to the newest intended version
- `ReadLints` reports no new diagnostics for edited model files
